MENTOR: Great, we'll work on Title.

This is the comp at **1 s**, halfway through Title's animation. "An easing lesson" is still faint because it's partway through fading in. Between **0.5 s and 1.5 s**, Title moves, scales up and fades in all at once. Then Position keeps going until **3 s**.

All four pairs are **linear** right now. Each value changes at the same speed the whole way, so Title starts moving at full speed with no build-up and stops dead at the next key. That's why it looks mechanical.

**Easing** fixes this. Title starts slowly, speeds up, and then slows down as it reaches each key, the way real objects move.

**How to do it:**
1. Select the Title layer and press **U** to show its keyframes.
2. Select the keys you want to ease.
3. Go to **Animation > Keyframe Assistant > Easy Ease**, or press **F9**.
4. The keyframe icons will change from diamonds to hourglass shapes. To check the motion, open the **Graph Editor** (the little graph icon above the timeline). Linear motion shows up as straight lines with sharp corners. Eased motion shows up as smooth S-curves.

**Your turn.** Ease all four of Title's pairs:
- **Position**, 0.5 s → 1.5 s
- **Position**, 1.5 s → 3 s
- **Scale**, 0.5 s → 1.5 s
- **Opacity**, 0.5 s → 1.5 s

Say **"done"** when you're ready and I'll check your work. If you'd like me to show you one first, just ask.

